<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Forge solver lab</title>
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><style>__STYLE__</style>
<main id="workspace"><div id="scene"><div id="axis-labels"></div><div class="scene-caption">SKELLYFORGE <span id="scene-title">Solver lab</span><small>Grid: 100 mm · XY plane at Z = 0</small></div></div>
<div id="plot-divider" role="separator" aria-orientation="horizontal" aria-label="Resize time series panels" tabindex="0"></div>
<div id="time-series"><div class="plot-toolbar"><strong>Time series</strong><label>Segment <select id="plot-body"></select></label>
<label style="color:#ff6464"><input id="plot-x" type="checkbox" checked>X</label>
<label style="color:#69d488"><input id="plot-y" type="checkbox" checked>Y</label>
<label style="color:#669fff"><input id="plot-z" type="checkbox" checked>Z</label>
<label style="color:#b8c2d1"><input id="plot-w" type="checkbox" checked>W (quaternion)</label>
<label>Landmark <select id="plot-point"><option>0</option><option>1</option><option>2</option><option>3</option><option>4</option><option>5</option><option>6</option><option>7</option></select></label>
</div><p class="plot-help">Solid: selected fit. Dashed: known. Dots: observed landmark. Amber shading: observation gap. Drag to zoom; scroll to zoom; use the toolbar to pan or reset. Click a data point to select a frame. Drag each panel's bottom-right corner to resize it, or Expand it. Quaternion components are unitless, not angles.</p>
<div class="plot-panels"><article id="video-panel" hidden><div class="plot-heading"><h3>Annotated recording / matched frame</h3><button id="video-collapse" aria-expanded="true">Collapse</button><button id="video-expand">Expand</button></div><label>Camera <select id="video-camera"></select></label><div id="video-series" class="plot-chart"><img id="annotated-frame" alt="Annotated camera frame" hidden></div><output id="video-value"></output></article><article id="problem-panel"><div class="plot-heading"><h3>Ceres problem / parameter and residual blocks</h3><button id="problem-collapse" aria-expanded="true">Collapse</button><button id="problem-expand">Expand</button></div><p id="problem-summary"></p><p id="map-scope"></p><div class="map-toolbar"><button id="map-fit">Fit all</button><button id="map-zoom-in" aria-label="Zoom in">+</button><button id="map-zoom-out" aria-label="Zoom out">-</button><button id="map-clear">Clear selection</button><label><input id="map-all" type="checkbox">All connections</label><span id="map-zoom"></span></div><details class="map-filters"><summary>Filter block types (display only)</summary><div class="map-toolbar"><button id="map-types-all">All types</button><button id="map-types-parameters">Parameters only</button><button id="map-types-motion">Motion residuals only</button></div><div id="map-filters" class="map-legend"></div><small>Connections appear only when both blocks are visible. Solver counts remain totals.</small></details><div id="problem-series" class="plot-chart" tabindex="0" aria-label="Ceres map: drag to pan, wheel to zoom, select a block to trace its connections"></div><output id="problem-selection" aria-live="polite">Hover a block to trace connections. Click to pin. Drag background to pan; wheel to zoom.</output><details class="map-explanation"><summary>Problem definition and scope</summary><output id="problem-value"></output></details></article><article id="chest-line-panel" hidden><div class="plot-heading"><h3>Chest from centerline / mm ? red: lateral; green: anterior (+), posterior (-)</h3><button id="chest-line-collapse" aria-expanded="true">Collapse</button><button id="chest-line-expand">Expand</button></div><div id="chest-line-series" class="plot-chart"></div><output id="chest-line-value"></output></article><article id="length-panel" hidden><div class="plot-heading"><h3>Spine lengths / mm ? green: sacrolumbar; blue: thoracic</h3><button id="length-collapse" aria-expanded="true">Collapse</button><button id="length-expand">Expand</button></div><div id="length-series" class="plot-chart"></div><output id="length-value"></output></article><article id="displacement-panel" hidden><div class="plot-heading"><h3>Linkage displacement / mm</h3><button id="displacement-collapse" aria-expanded="true">Collapse</button><button id="displacement-expand">Expand</button></div><div id="displacement-series" class="plot-chart"></div><output id="displacement-value"></output></article><article id="translation-panel"><div class="plot-heading"><h3>Translation / mm</h3><button id="translation-collapse" aria-expanded="true">Collapse</button><button id="translation-expand">Expand</button></div><div id="translation-series" class="plot-chart" aria-label="translation time series"></div><output id="translation-value"></output></article>
<article id="rotation-panel"><div class="plot-heading"><h3>Quaternion / WXYZ</h3><button id="rotation-collapse" aria-expanded="true">Collapse</button><button id="rotation-expand">Expand</button></div><div id="rotation-series" class="plot-chart" aria-label="rotation time series"></div><output id="rotation-value"></output></article>
<article id="point-panel"><div class="plot-heading"><h3>Landmark world position / mm</h3><button id="point-collapse" aria-expanded="true">Collapse</button><button id="point-expand">Expand</button></div><div id="point-series" class="plot-chart" aria-label="point time series"></div><output id="point-value"></output></article></div></div></main>
<div id="divider" role="separator" aria-label="Resize controls panel" aria-orientation="vertical" aria-controls="panel" tabindex="0" title="Drag to resize · arrow keys to adjust · double-click to reset"></div>
<aside id="panel"><header><span class="eyebrow">SKELLYFORGE / SOLVER LAB</span><h2>Fitting experiments</h2><span class="badge">Ceres ? quaternion poses</span></header>
<section><h3>Experiment</h3>
<label>Example <select id="experiment"></select></label><p id="experiment-description"></p>
<div id="experiment-controls"></div>
<label id="mode-label">Fitting method <select id="mode"></select></label>
<div id="playback"><div class="actions"><button id="play">Play</button><button id="previous">Previous</button><button id="next">Next</button></div><input id="frame" type="range" min="0" max="40" value="0" step="1" aria-label="Frame"><p id="clock"></p><label id="recording-frame-label" hidden>Recording frame <input id="recording-frame" type="number" step="1"></label></div>
<p>Controls select actual saved Ceres solves. No fitting or geometry corrections happen in this page.</p>
</section><section><h3>Scene layers</h3><label>Body region (Ceres map and axes) <select id="body-region"></select></label><label>Segment focus (Ceres map and axes) <select id="body-focus"></select></label><label>Segment colors <select id="segment-colors"><option value="model">Rigid / variable length</option><option value="support">Direct measurement support</option><option value="segments">Individual segments</option></select></label><p id="segment-legend"></p>
<label><input type="checkbox" id="grid" checked> Ground grid · Z = 0</label>
<label><input type="checkbox" id="truth" checked> Known pose: wireframe segments; cyan landmarks</label>
<label><input type="checkbox" id="initial"> Gray: selected method's initial pose</label>
<label><input type="checkbox" id="fitted" checked> Fit: solid segment colors; orange landmarks; purple withheld landmarks</label>
<label><input type="checkbox" id="observed" checked> Pink markers: observed targets (large wire spheres for real data)</label>
<label><input type="checkbox" id="residuals" checked> Pink lines: fitted landmark → target</label>
<label><input type="checkbox" id="axes" checked> Local XYZ axes (red/green/blue)</label>
<label><input type="checkbox" id="contextSegments" checked> Gray: saved full-body segments (context, not fitted)</label>
<label><input type="checkbox" id="chestCenterline" checked> Yellow: hip/shoulder centerline; pink: chest displacement</label>
<label><input type="checkbox" id="contextKeypoints" checked> Small cyan spheres: saved full-body keypoints</label>
<label><input type="checkbox" id="contextLandmarks"> Wire spheres: saved full-body landmarks</label>
<div class="actions"><button id="reset">Reset camera</button><button id="download">Download run JSON</button></div>
<details open><summary>How to read this scene</summary><p><b>Real recording:</b> colored tapered bones are the segments included in the selected Ceres experiment. Faint gray sticks are saved full-body context, not fitted here. The selected experiment declares which mapped keypoints supply targets: large pink wire spheres are observed targets; orange solid spheres are fitted landmark positions; pink connectors show their error. Small cyan dots are the remaining saved keypoints.</p><p><b>Slim sticks with endpoint spheres</b>: rigid segment axes and linkage attachments. Segments in selector order: amber, green, blue, pink, light cyan. Small dots at box corners: landmarks. The box edges show rigid local landmark geometry.</p><p><b>Segments:</b> solid sticks/spheres are fitted; wireframe outlines are known. <b>Landmarks:</b> cyan wireframe is known; orange solid is fitted. Pink dots: noisy observations. Purple dots: fitted landmarks with observations withheld. Cyan shells surrounding orange dots mean close agreement; separation is fit error against known truth.</p><p>The first linkage stays joined by construction. At the second linkage, a <b>gold line between attachment spheres</b> shows allowed displacement along middle local Z. That gap is modeled motion, not attachment-equation error. Compare its fitted value with the known value in the displacement plot.</p><p>Small cyan/orange differences are expected with noise and temporal/prior residuals. Turn off Known pose to inspect the fit alone. Surface overlap can flicker; it does not by itself mean unstable motion.</p></details><p>Drag to orbit; scroll to zoom. Hover a landmark for its identity and coordinates. Coordinates and residuals are millimeters.</p>
</section><section><h3>Fit diagnostics</h3><pre id="status"></pre><p id="observability" hidden></p><pre id="sequence-status"></pre><details><summary>Objective and solver settings</summary><pre id="settings"></pre><h3>Objective by iteration</h3><p id="objective-caption">Selected-frame squared landmark error.</p><svg id="cost" viewBox="0 0 340 90" role="img" aria-label="Solver objective by iteration"></svg>
</details><details><summary>Landmark residuals ? selected segment</summary><table><thead><tr><th>Landmark</th><th>Residual (mm)</th></tr></thead><tbody id="errors"></tbody></table></details>
<details><summary>Quaternions and translations</summary><pre id="poses"></pre></details>
<p>The known pose is used only to generate data and evaluate error. It is not supplied to the fit. Missing targets are omitted, not interpolated.</p>
</section></aside><div id="tooltip" hidden></div><script>__ASSETS__</script><script>const EXPERIMENTS=__EXPERIMENTS__;</script><script>__VIEWER__</script></html>
